WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:07.809
When she fell into the salt water, Alice thought she had fallen into the sea.

2
00:00:07.829 --> 00:00:09.510
But she soon realized she was in a pool of her own tears.

3
00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:16.132
"I cried all these tears when I was nine feet high," Alice said.

4
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:39.743
She swam about, trying to find her way to dry land.

5
00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:46.528
wish I hadn't cried so much.

6
00:00:47.429 --> 00:00:49.931
I'll be punished for that by drowning in my own tears.

7
00:00:50.832 --> 00:00:54.314
That will be strange indeed, but everything is strange today."

8
00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:59.098
Just then Alice heard something splashing.

9
00:00:59.999 --> 00:01:02.981
At first she thought it must be a walrus or a hippo.

10
00:01:03.842 --> 00:01:06.124
But then she remembered how small she was.

11
00:01:06.988 --> 00:01:08.609
The creature must be small too.

12
00:01:10.791 --> 00:01:16.314
Alice swam toward the sound and soon spotted a mouse, which had also fallen into the pool.

13
00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:20.377
"Is there any point in speaking to this creature?"

14
00:01:20.877 --> 00:01:21.518
Alice thought.

15
00:01:21.538 --> 00:01:23.919
"Can he even understand me?

16
00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:28.502
Everything is so strange down here that he probably can talk."

17
00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:32.585
She decided to take a chance and speak to him.

18
00:01:32.605 --> 00:01:35.347
"Oh, Mouse!"

19
00:01:35.867 --> 00:01:36.528
Alice called.

20
00:01:37.432 --> 00:01:39.053
"Do you know the way out of this pool?

21
00:01:39.914 --> 00:01:41.595
I'm very tired of swimming.

22
00:01:41.615 --> 00:01:43.877
Oh, Mouse!"

23
00:01:45.558 --> 00:01:48.140
The Mouse looked at Alice with some interest.

24
00:01:49.101 --> 00:01:51.883
He also seemed to wink at her but said nothing.

25
00:01:51.903 --> 00:01:57.847
"Hmm. Perhaps he doesn't understand English," Alice said to herself.

26
00:01:58.628 --> 00:01:59.969
"Maybe he's from France."

27
00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:03.492
Alice decided to try speaking some French.

28
00:02:04.528 --> 00:02:08.409
All she could think of was the first sentence in her French grammar book.

29
00:02:09.609 --> 00:02:14.331
Unfortunately, that sentence was "Where is my cat?"

30
00:02:15.131 --> 00:02:19.652
The Mouse gave a sudden leap out of the water and quivered with fright.

31
00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:22.593
"Oh, I'm so sorry!"

32
00:02:22.993 --> 00:02:23.933
Alice said quickly.

33
00:02:23.953 --> 00:02:26.534
"I forgot that mice dislike cats."

34
00:02:26.554 --> 00:02:29.295
"Dislike cats?"

35
00:02:29.575 --> 00:02:30.455
the Mouse cried.

36
00:02:30.475 --> 00:02:33.216
"Would you like cats, if you were me?"

37
00:02:34.912 --> 00:02:39.233
"Well, perhaps not, but don't be angry with me," Alice said calmly.

38
00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.114
She was glad that the Mouse spoke English.

39
00:02:42.134 --> 00:02:45.015
"I wish that I could show you my cat, Dinah.

40
00:02:45.835 --> 00:02:47.955
I think you'd learn to like cats if you met her.

41
00:02:48.996 --> 00:02:51.096
Dinah is such a dear, quiet thing."

42
00:02:52.737 --> 00:02:54.057
The Mouse said nothing.

43
00:02:55.998 --> 00:03:00.619
Alice swam lazily around the pool as she described Dinah for the Mouse.

44
00:03:01.499 --> 00:03:04.620
"Dinah lies by the fire, purring so nicely.

45
00:03:05.728 --> 00:03:07.709
She licks her paws and washes her face.

46
00:03:09.069 --> 00:03:11.030
She's such a nice, soft thing to pet.

47
00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:20.794
And she's the best at catching mice The Mouse was shaking with anger, and Alice was sure she

48
00:03:20.855 --> 00:03:21.595
had offended him.

49
00:03:21.615 --> 00:03:24.496
"Oh, I beg your pardon," Alice said.

50
00:03:24.516 --> 00:03:27.057
"We won't talk about Dinah anymore."

51
00:03:27.077 --> 00:03:30.539
"We!" the Mouse squeaked.

52
00:03:30.559 --> 00:03:33.480
"As if I would talk about such a thing!

53
00:03:34.384 --> 00:03:37.026
Our family has always hated cats.

54
00:03:37.926 --> 00:03:39.907
Don't let me hear that word again."

55
00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:49.253
right," Alice said as she desperately tried to think of another topic of conversation.

56
00:03:49.273 --> 00:03:52.274
"How about dogs?

57
00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:53.535
Are you fond of dogs?"

58
00:03:54.355 --> 00:03:58.998
The Mouse did not reply, so Alice went on eagerly.

59
00:03:59.018 --> 00:04:02.080
"There's such a nice dog on the farm near our house.

60
00:04:02.964 --> 00:04:04.606
It fetches things when you throw them.

61
00:04:07.028 --> 00:04:08.889
And it sits up and begs for its dinner.

62
00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:11.431
The farmer says it's worth a lot of money.

63
00:04:12.332 --> 00:04:17.997
That's because it's so good at catching rats, and—" The Mouse started swimming away from Alice as fast

64
00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:18.757
as he could.

65
00:04:18.777 --> 00:04:26.023
"Oh, no, I'm afraid I've hurt his feelings again," Alice said in a sad voice.

66
00:04:27.524 --> 00:04:31.508
She decided to try one more time to make friends with the frightened animal.

67
00:04:33.288 --> 00:04:34.229
"Mouse, dear!"

68
00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:35.791
Alice called softly.

69
00:04:35.811 --> 00:04:40.936
"If you come back, I promise we won't talk about dogs or cats anymore."
